  "text_md": "tbr\n\n![](<83b820be15e1c897ebdfb9ac6ecfa4d499e2_pg1_pg1_images/imageFile1.png>)\n\nSuccess at Chattanooga State\n\n# 1,473\n\nDegrees & Certificates Awarded in 2019-20\n\n# 51.5%\n\nFirst-Year Retention Rate for the 2018 Cohort\n\n22.0%\n\nThree-Year Graduation Rate for the 2017 Cohort\n\n# Chattanooga State Community College\n\n2021 Student Success Profile\n\n# First-Time, Full-Time Freshmen\n\n<table>\n  <tr>\n    <th>Total Cohort</th>\n    <th>Fall 2015 1,837 students</th>\n    <th>Fall 2016 1,600 students</th>\n    <th>Fall 2017 1,589 students</th>\n    <th>Fall 2018 1,722 students</th>\n    <th>Fall 2019 1,590 students</th>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>White</td>\n    <td>76%</td>\n    <td>74%</td>\n    <td>74%</td>\n    <td>73%</td>\n    <td>67%</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>Black</td>\n    <td>14%</td>\n    <td>14%</td>\n    <td>14%</td>\n    <td>13%</td>\n    <td>17%</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>Hispanic</td>\n    <td>14%</td>\n    <td>7%</td>\n    <td>7%</td>\n    <td>7%</td>\n    <td> </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>Hispanic Pell Recipients</td>\n    <td>4% 57%</td>\n    <td>7% 58%</td>\n    <td>7% 57%</td>\n    <td>7% 57%</td>\n    <td>60%</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>ACT Below 19</td>\n    <td>40%</td>\n    <td>39%</td>\n    <td>39%</td>\n    <td>37%</td>\n    <td>42%</td>\n  </tr>\n</table>\n\n\nThe first-time, full-time cohort includes degree-seeking students who enroll in college for the first time in fall (or in the prior summer and continued in the fall) and attempted at least 12 hours.\n\n# Three-Year Graduation Rate\n\n![](<83b820be15e1c897ebdfb9ac6ecfa4d499e2_pg1_pg1_images/imageFile2.png>)\n\n25%\n\n22%\n\n21%\n\n20%\n\n15%\n\n17%\n\n10%\n\n13%\n\n5%\n\n0%\n\n2013-16\n\n2014-17\n\n2015-18\n\n2016-19\n\n2017-20\n\n![](<83b820be15e1c897ebdfb9ac6ecfa4d499e2_pg1_pg1_images/imageFile3.png>)\n\n# Success for the 2017 Freshman Cohort\n\n23%\n\n14%\n\n12%\n\nGraduated from\n\nTransferred to Another Institution\n\nStill Enrolled\n\nAny\n\nCollege\n\nafter 3 Years\n\nSuccess for the 2017 cohort includes the percent of students who earned a degree or certificate from any institution within or outside the TBR system, transferred to another institution, or were still enrolled as of summer 2020\n\n![](<83b820be15e1c897ebdfb9ac6ecfa4d499e2_pg1_pg1_images/imageFile4.png>)\n\n# Cumulative Graduation Rate\n\nCohort\n\n2018\n\n25%\n\n2017\n\n2016\n\n2015\n\n15%\n\n2014\n\n10%\n\n2013\n\n5%\n\n2012\n\n2011\n\n0%\n\n11\n\n13\n\n15\n\n17\n\n19\n\n21\n\n23\n\n25\n\n27\n\n9\n\nCalendar Semesters\n\n",
